  (i) **the cap is per REQUEST, the limiter is 60 requests/min per address:** 60 × 10 = **600 entries/min ≥ the 500-entry ring — one address still replaces the
  whole ring in 50 requests (< 1 min)**; before RD-618 (`1904765`, 1 entry per request) it took 500 requests (~8.3 min). A-F1's oracle was *"F-A2's own
  concern"* and *"the limiter's stated contract (60/min per address)"*: **say whether A-F1 is CLOSED or narrowed to a 10× residue (severity yours).**
  (ii) the cap line counts `offered` BEFORE `isEmptyCspEntry` and the `r.body` object check, so **an array of report objects with empty bodies (or no
  `body`) logs "kept 0 of M … (per-request cap)" when no cap applied** — a log line that is not true (predict: logged; the request then 400 per R2's path).
  (iii) `buildCspEntry` still runs on EVERY array item before `.slice` (work is not capped, only storage; READ; Polish).
  (iv) **the userinfo regex needs `[^/?#]*@`: userinfo that CONTAINS `?` or `#`** (`https://qab9u:pa?ss@h.test:99999/x`) **fails the regex, and the `[?#]` cut
  then keeps `https://qab9u:pa`** — the user name and part of the password survive (predict KEPT). **A value with leading whitespace/C0 before the scheme**
  (` https://qab9u:pw@h.test/x`) fails the scheme pre-test, so neither `new URL` nor the regex runs (predict userinfo KEPT; `new URL` itself would trim it).
  **A backslash authority** (`https:\\qab9u:pw@h.test:99999\x`) — predict KEPT. **A `blob:` wrapper around an unparseable inner URL** — predict DROPPED
  (`blob:` parses; the inner value takes the fallback). Browsers strip userinfo, so these are forged reports only (batch 7 rated A-F2 Minor on that basis).
  (v) **the discriminator is now `typeof err.type === 'string'`, not body-parser's own:** ANY typed error reaching the intake is answered with its
  `err.status` (or 400) and no body. RD-646/647's named error has NO `type` and sets `statusCode = 503` (READ at `608a1cd` server :1175-1182, no `.status`) — so
  a future `type` on it would turn the named 503 into a bare 400 from the intake (row x4 measures that the census reddens).
  (vi) **"type-less errors still go to next()" is guarded by NO cell in rd618 alone** (READ: R5/R7 are typed): only the cross tree's CENSUS can see it (x3).
